-- hvac-tests-red.l4 -- EXPECTATIONS THAT ARE MEANT TO FAIL.  Thirteen assertions, all of which
-- are expected to print "assertion failed"; check.sh counts them (expected_failed = 13).
-- F1 to F7 are the first run's; F8 to F13 were added by the date correction (the last section).
--
-- Each is an expectation transcribed from the SimpLEX screenshot, run against a vintage that does
-- not meet it.  They are findings, not bugs: no expected value here was edited to match the
-- code, and keeping them in their own file doubles as proof that the harness can fail.
--
--   F1-F4  the draft's table run against the regulations as made / as amended
--   F5-F7  the worked example's result, "registration rejected, payment must be completed",
--          which the table's own row 8 contradicts ("service suspension") for the same facts
--
-- Expected values are the panel's outcome words, not anything the encoding computed.

§ `Table rows that the regulations as made do not meet`

-- F1  Row 5 expects "registration approved" for a theory exam.  The regulations as made have no
--     theory exam (not defined, not priced): the vintage is silent, NOTHING, not approval.
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `As made` `for` `row 5: registration for a theory exam` EQUALS JUST `registration approved`
-- F2  Row 7 on a theory exam: no theory exam, so no objection fee for it.
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `As made` `for` `row 7: an appeal with payment, on a theory exam` EQUALS JUST `the appeal is examined`
-- F3  Row 8 on a theory exam: no fee is set, so regulation 4 conditions nothing.
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `As made` `for` `row 8: registration for a theory exam without payment` EQUALS JUST `service suspension`

§ `Table rows that the regulations as amended do not meet`

-- F4  Row 7 on a practical exam: the 5786 amendment narrowed 2(ב) to the THEORY exam score.
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `As amended` `for` `row 7: an appeal with payment, on a practical exam` EQUALS JUST `the appeal is examined`

§ `The worked example's result, against all three vintages`

-- F5  Draft.  Same facts as row 8 (a candidate registers for a theory exam and does not pay), but
--     the example's result is "registration rejected, payment must be completed" where row 8's is
--     "service suspension".  One function cannot return both; it returns row 8's.
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` Draft `for` `the worked example` EQUALS JUST `registration rejected, payment must be completed`
-- F6  As made: no theory exam, silent.
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `As made` `for` `the worked example` EQUALS JUST `registration rejected, payment must be completed`
-- F7  As amended: the theory exam is priced and regulation 4 bites, but the word is again row 8's.
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `As amended` `for` `the worked example` EQUALS JUST `registration rejected, payment must be completed`

§ `Readings that Interpretation Law s 10 excludes (F8 to F12) or leaves open (F13)`

-- Added by the date correction.  Each asserts the answer of a reading this encoding considered,
-- decided from the statute and not from the code, and each fails because the encoded reading is the
-- other one.  Five of them were forks (F-D3, F-D4, F-R5) while the sources did not state how a period
-- is counted; Interpretation Law s 10 states it, so they are now readings the statute excludes.

-- F8  s 10(b): three years from the Commencement Day, 16 July 2025.  The reading that "from" includes
--     the day, so that the period ends the day before the third anniversary, would end it on 15 July
--     2028.  s 10(b) puts the last day on the day with the event day's number (the Interpretation
--     row's R3, rejected there too).
#ASSERT `the last day of the three-year rows of the Second Schedule` EQUALS YMD 2028 7 15
-- F9  s 10(a): thirty days from the change on 1 March 2026.  Counting 1 March as the first day would
--     end the period on 30 March.  s 10(a): "אותו יום לא יבוא במנין" -- that day is not counted; the
--     last day is 31 March.
#ASSERT `s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` (`Change of details` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), NOTHING, TRUE) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 30
-- F10 s 10(a): seven days from the publication on 9 July 2025.  Counting 9 July as the first day
--     would put the commencement on 15 July 2025; s 10(a) excludes it (reg 5, fork F-R5).
#ASSERT `the day the principal regulations commenced` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 15
-- F11 s 10(b): five years from a grant on 15 January 2025.  The five-year limb ends on 15 January
--     2030, inside the period; "the day before the fifth anniversary", 14 January 2030, is the
--     same mistake as F8.
#ASSERT `the end of the five-year limb for a period beginning on` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 14
-- F12 s 10(b): 18 months from the Commencement Day.  "The day before" would put the Law's commencement
--     for work on any other refrigerant on 15 January 2027; the last day of the period is 16 January.
#ASSERT `the day the Law commences for` `work on a system using any other refrigerant` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 15
-- F13 s 10(c), several days of rest in a row at the end (the Interpretation row's F3, left OPEN
--     there).  Thirty days from the change on 5 March 2026 nominally end on Saturday 4 April 2026;
--     with Friday 3 April and Saturday 4 April both days of rest the encoded reading (the module's
--     reading A) extends to the first day that is not one, Sunday 5 April.  The replacement reading
--     (reading B: each trailing rest day is made up by one more day) gives Monday 6 April.  This
--     fails because A is encoded; it is NOT a finding that B is wrong, which the text does not settle.
#ASSERT (`s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` (`Change of details` OF (YMD 2026 3 5), NOTHING, TRUE) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 6
